<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX5-QA1-006>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX5-QA1-006" ;
  triage:title "last_task_attempt map is never pruned or capped and grows unboundedly for a churning roster" ;
  triage:description "AX.5 QA-1 (quality-mgr ax5-qa-r1, PR #1201 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T12:38Z) at head da823baaa0018933f8daac388733c51eb14e9335. rust-service-hardening-agent RSH-001: last_task_attempt: Arc<Mutex<HashMap<MemberKey, IsoTimestamp>>> (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs:68) has no removal path or cap, so it grows for the daemon's lifetime as roster members churn, unlike the bounded RuntimeHealth member cache pattern in the same crate. Fix: prune entries for members no longer in the roster on each tick (or bound the map), with a test." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
